<!-- ── §02 ── -->
<section id="s-denoising" data-code="denoising">
<div class="section-no">02 — Masked Diffusion Primer</div>
<h2>How dLLMs Iteratively Unmask Text</h2>
<p>Unlike autoregressive LLMs that output one token at a time from left to right, diffusion LLMs start with a fully masked sequence and progressively reveal tokens over T denoising steps. At each step, the model predicts all token positions simultaneously, then keeps only the top-k most confident predictions — unmasking the tokens it's most certain about first.</p>

<div class="math-block">
  <div class="math-label">Forward process — corrupts clean response y₀ to masked yₜ</div>
  <span class="math-var">q(yₜ | y₀, x)</span> = ∏ᵢ <span class="math-var">qₜ(yₜⁱ | y₀ⁱ)</span>
  <span class="math-comment"> ← each token independently masked with prob t/T</span><br>
  <span class="math-var">Pₜⁱ</span> = <span class="math-var">pθ(yⁱ | yₜ, x)</span>, 1 ≤ i ≤ L
  <span class="math-comment"> ← model scores all positions at step t</span>
</div>

<p>The interactive canvas below shows denoising in action. Press <strong>Play</strong> to watch the model unmask a GSM8K-style reasoning chain step by step — the most confident tokens (🟢 green) are revealed first, while uncertain positions stay masked (⬜ grey).</p>

<div class="vp">
  <div class="vp-head">
    <span class="vp-title">dLLM denoising — iterative unmasking</span>
    <span class="vp-hint">click Play to run T steps</span>
  </div>
  <div class="vp-body">
    <div style="margin-bottom:.75rem;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.5rem">
      <div style="font-size:.75rem;font-family:var(--ff-mono);color:var(--cyan)">Q: Janet earns $25/hr. She works 8 hrs. How much does she earn?</div>
