      <strong>Why ρ=0.25 beats ρ=0.50 in practice:</strong> Even though ρ=0.50 gives a stronger teacher (93.4% vs 94.8%), ρ=0.25 achieves slightly better final performance. The <em>gap</em> between student and teacher matters more than raw teacher strength — too much future revelation collapses the learning signal.
